 "description": "Jiang2007 - GSIS system, Pancreatic Beta Cells\nBioModels BIOMD0000000239 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000239_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 300 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000239_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: oscillating), sampling 0.3.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 4.95e-06 of species peak (worst: FAD)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] v1: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v4: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v6: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v8: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v9: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v10: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v11: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - Cit: zero order, signed\n  [info] v12: rate not proportional to its reactants; written once as signed lines (source+S[USER;...]) for IsoCit, NAD_p\n  [info] v14: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] v15: USER expression is 1013 characters; Kintecus V2027 mis-evaluates USER expressions longer than about 840 characters (see KINTECUS_ISSUES)\n  [info] v15 (consumes GDP): USER expression is 10